  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Initiating Execution Phase**\n\nOkay, the plan is approved, and we\'re entering Phase 3: Execution! I\'m now reviewing the required features and specifications. \"PlayThat!\" will be the application\'s name, complete with a custom icon and branding. I\'m focusing on the metadata and HTML requirements, specifically the `/metadata.json` file.\n\n\n**Defining Core Features**\n\nI\'ve specified the core features, including the unique brand icon (a layered play prism with neon speed waves and a privacy shield), and the Android shell with adaptive modes, along with MX Player-style gesture controls. I\'m focusing on the video engine and its controls, including brightness and volume adjustments. I\'m also planning the subtitle support and stream conversion capabilities.\n\n\n**Refining Playback Controls**\n\nI\'m now detailing the MX Player-style gesture controls, including fast scrubbing with delta badges and double-tap actions for play/pause and seeking. I\'m also planning a screen lock toggle, decoder options (HW, HW+, SW), and varied playback speeds. Aspect ratio controls, PiP, fullscreen, and a sleep timer are included. I\'m further specifying the audio track selector and subtitle engine details.\n\n\n**Detailing Subtitle Options**\n\nI\'m currently designing the subtitle customization modal, with options for font size (14px to 36px), various font families and colors, as well as outline and shadow styling. I\'m also finalizing the vertical positioning options, background box opacity settings, and Subtitle Delay Sync adjustments, allowing precise timing shifts in 100ms increments.\n\n\\n\\n\n\n**Implementing Media Sniffer**\n\nI\'ve moved on to the in-app Chromium-style browser and M3U8 downloader. I\'m focusing on the address bar with search and navigation. I\'m also working on quick bookmarks, and the active media sniffer for detecting `.m3u8` playlists and media URLs. I\'m planning a segment-by-segment HLS downloader to fetch TS segments, show live progress and estimate remaining time.\n\n\n**Adding Security Layers**\n\nI\'m now integrating robust security measures. I\'m focusing on the encrypted database storage vault, using client-side AES-256-GCM encryption with PBKDF2 for key derivation based on a user-provided PIN or pattern. I\'m also implementing an emergency disguise button that turns the interface into a fully functional calculator, with a secret unlock code for instant vault access. Furthermore, I\'m designing a biometric and PIN unlock modal with failed attempt feedback.\n\n\n"
