  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Media Item Types**\n\nI\'m currently focused on defining the `MediaItem` type within `src/types/index.ts`. This involves specifying properties like `id`, `title`, `folder`, and `sourceType` (which can be \'local\', \'stream\', or \'downloaded\'). I\'m also including `url`, `blobKey`, `thumbnailUrl`, `duration`, `currentTime`, and `resolution` to capture essential media details.\n\n\n**Expanding Media Metadata**\n\nI\'ve been expanding the media item types, adding properties like `fileSize`, `codec`, `decoder`, and `isEncrypted`. I\'m also working on `FolderItem`, `Playlist`, `SubtitleTrack`, and `SubtitleSettings` types. The details for `M3U8StreamInfo` and `DownloadProgress` are also coming along, along with `DecoderMode` and `AspectRatio`. Finally, I\'m working to make sure to include `createdAt` and `lastPlayedAt`.\n\n\n**Implementing Secure Features**\n\nI\'m now integrating security measures. I\'m focusing on implementing secure salt and hash methods. I\'m also addressing vault lock state management and auto-lock timeout functionality. This is a recent addition.\n\n\n**Defining Default User Experience**\n\nI\'m now thinking about default folder organization: \"Camera,\" \"Downloads,\" \"Stream Captures,\" \"Movies,\" and a \"Private Vault\" are the initial options. I\'m moving toward an Android-style UI with `AndroidFrame.tsx`, featuring a status bar (time, battery, Wi-Fi, 5G), a dynamic camera cutout, and a gesture navigation bar. I\'m focusing on responsiveness, with phone, tablet, and full-screen modes. I\'m planning for a flagship player experience, `MXPlayer.tsx`, with dual-zone gestures.\n\n\n**Designing Player Control Features**\n\nI\'m now implementing the player controls. I\'ve defined rewind/forward gestures and pinch-to-zoom/aspect ratio cycling. I\'m building out a hardware acceleration switch with `HW`, `HW+` (enhanced WebGL filters), and `SW` modes. I\'m focusing on real-time subtitle rendering with custom styles. I\'m designing an on-screen controls overlay, including a top bar with back, title, decoder, audio, subtitle and more controls. The center will have a large play/pause button and gesture HUDs. Finally, I\'m integrating a bottom bar with time, seek, play/pause, next/previous, lock, aspect ratio and fullscreen toggles. I\'m also including an interactive live subtitle preview modal with a font size slider in `src/components/SubtitleCustomizerModal.tsx`.\n\n\n**Refining Subtitle Options**\n\nI\'m currently perfecting the subtitle customization features. I\'ve got font size ranging from 12px to 38px, a text color picker, and background opacity controls from transparent to solid black. I\'m also including outline styles, vertical positioning, and a delay sync slider. There will be \"Reset\" and \"Test\" buttons for the sync slider. Additionally, I\'m integrating external subtitle import for `.srt` and `.vtt` files. I\'m building this into `src/components/SubtitleCustomizerModal.tsx`.\n\nI\'m now implementing the in-app browser features. This will be Chromium-based, with standard controls and a bookmarks bar. I\'m also preparing a streaming website catalog. Finally, I\'m working on an automated stream sniffer to detect media streams and offer a one-click download option, along with a live segment downloader with progress details. This will be `src/components/InAppBrowser.tsx`.\n\n\n**Adding Vault Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating the Private Vault. I\'m focusing on an Android-style PIN entry and an optional 3x3 pattern lock. I\'m designing an Emergency Disguise Mode, making the screen appear as a working calculator. Entering the secret code unlocks the vault. I\'m also implementing an encrypted media list with options for adding, exporting, playing, and decrypting files within the vault. I\'m also including a \"Play in PlayThat!\" button on the download button.\n\n\n\n"
