  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Tab Functionality**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `src/components/InAppBrowser.tsx` file, specifically how it handles the browser\'s state. It currently manages a single active URL. To support multiple tabs, I\'m thinking about how to refactor this component to accommodate a collection of URLs and states, considering a maximum of forty tabs as the user requested.\n\n\n**Designing Tab Implementation**\n\nI\'ve sketched out a `BrowserTab` interface to model tab state with `id`, `title`, `url`, and more, including stream detection. I am setting a maximum of forty tabs using `MAX_TABS = 40`, and implemented a UI to show tab counts. Desktop and tablet will use a horizontal tab bar, while mobile will get a tab switcher grid and the Android-style badge.\n\n\n"
