  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Component Integration**\n\nI\'m currently integrating the `EnhancementsModal` component into `MXPlayer.tsx`. I\'ve added the import statement, bringing in `EnhancementConfig` and `DEFAULT_ENHANCEMENTS` as well. Now, I\'m defining the `MXPlayerProps` interface to ensure type safety and proper data flow within the component. This is setting the stage for integrating enhancements.\n\n\n**Refining State Management**\n\nI\'ve just added `enhancements` and `isEnhancementsModalOpen` to state, using `useState` within `MXPlayer`. I\'m setting the default `enhancements` to either the provided `enhancementConfig` or `DEFAULT_ENHANCEMENTS`. Also, I\'ve begun integrating the `getFilterStyle` function, incorporating the new `enhancements` state into the brightness, contrast, and saturation calculations, factoring in hardware decoding.\n\n\n**Implementing Visual Enhancements**\n\nI\'ve updated the `getFilterStyle` function to apply sharpness presets, adding `contrast`, `saturate`, and `brightness` adjustments based on the `sharpnessPreset` within the `enhancements` state. I\'ve integrated a button to trigger the enhancements modal in the top bar, utilizing a `Sparkles` icon and updating state on click. Also, I\'ve put a similar button inside the settings dropdown for direct access.\n\n\n**Integrating Enhancement Features**\n\nI\'ve integrated the enhancements modal, including event handlers to manage its visibility and data updates within `MXPlayer.tsx`. I\'m now passing in the `enhancements` config via props. I\'m also implementing the \"Audio & Video Enhancements\" button within the settings menu, which will trigger the modal. Also, I am now updating `App.tsx` and dynamically updating font scaling based on the enhancement config, so the font updates app-wide in real time.\n\n\n"
