  checkpoint {
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **App Name**: `PlayThat!` \342\200\223 An Android MX Player-inspired media player and stream downloader web application.\n- **Key Features Built & Required**:\n  - MX Player dual-zone gesture controls (left swipe: brightness, right swipe: volume with 200% boost, horizontal swipe: timeline seek, double-tap seek/pause, screen lock).\n  - Multi-format playback with `hls.js` (.m3u8, .mp4, .webm) and HW/HW+/SW decoder simulation.\n  - Subtitle customization (font size, color, background box, offset, delay sync, .srt/.vtt import).\n  - In-app Chromium browser with up to 40 tabs and automatic HLS stream sniffer.\n  - PlayThat! Download Manager (UC Browser-style Turbo mode, direct MP4 downloads, chunked progress).\n  - Download confirmation dialog allowing the user to customize the file name and destination path before downloading (download does **not** auto-start).\n  - Encrypted Private Vault (WebCrypto AES-256-GCM + PBKDF2 in IndexedDB) with PIN and Android Calculator emergency disguise.\n  - System adaptive font scaling (`clamp()` fluid base + Standard/Large/Extra Large toggle).\n  - **Immediate User Request to Implement**: Add a dedicated **Settings Tab** placed **after Playlists** in the bottom navigation bar matching the user\'s uploaded reference image (`/public/assets/aistudio/image_059c68a8.png`), strictly excluding \"Game Center\" and \"Subscription\" as requested.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed Components**:\n  - `src/types/index.ts`: Data models for `MediaItem`, `DownloadTask` (with `savePath`), `M3U8DownloadTask`, `SubtitleSettings`, `Playlist`.\n  - `src/services/cryptoVault.ts`: Full WebCrypto AES-GCM 256-bit encryption/decryption, PBKDF2 salt derivation, and IndexedDB storage.\n  - `src/services/m3u8Downloader.ts`: HLS manifest parser, segment downloader, and remuxer.\n  - `src/services/downloadManagerService.ts`: Download manager engine supporting direct MP4 and M3U8 chunked downloads with pause/resume and custom `savePath`.\n  - `src/services/subtitleParser.ts`: SRT & VTT parsers with real-time cue lookup and delay offset.\n  - `src/data/sampleMedia.ts`: Initial media catalog, stream bookmarks, and default subtitle styles.\n  - `src/components/PlayThatIcon.tsx`: Custom vector icon with glowing squircle and speed waves.\n  - `src/components/AndroidFrame.tsx`: Android phone/tablet mockup frame with status bar and gesture pill.\n  - `src/components/MXPlayer.tsx`: Flagship player with touch gestures, HUDs, subtitle overlay, decoder switcher, and A/V Enhancements integration.\n  - `src/components/SubtitleCustomizerModal.tsx`: Subtitle style customization and file upload modal.\n  - `src/components/InAppBrowser.tsx`: Multi-tab browser (up to 40 tabs) with Android tab grid switcher, stream sniffer, and manual download confirmation modal.\n  - `src/components/UCDownloadManager.tsx`: Branded \"PlayThat! Download Manager\" with Turbo Boost and path selection.\n  - `src/components/DownloadPromptModal.tsx`: Download confirmation sheet allowing users to change save destination path before downloads begin.\n  - `src/components/FileBrowser.tsx`: MX-style folder navigator with full-width complete-line search bar and dedicated action strip.\n  - `src/components/PlaylistManager.tsx`: Playlist creator, queue, and shuffle player.\n  - `src/components/PrivateVaultModal.tsx`: PIN authentication, AES-GCM encrypted list, and working Android Calculator disguise.\n  - `src/components/EnhancementsModal.tsx`: Audio & video enhancement studio (HW/HW+/SW, contrast/saturation, night mode, volume boost 200%, bass boost, clear voice, spatial stereo, equalizer, bluetooth delay, font scale).\n  - `src/index.css`: System-adaptive fluid typography and font scaling classes.\n- **Verification Status**:\n  - `tsc --noEmit` (`lint_applet`): Passed with 0 errors.\n  - `compile_applet`: Build succeeded.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Decisions\n- **Settings Screen Reference**: The user uploaded an MX Player settings screenshot (`/public/assets/aistudio/image_059c68a8.png`) featuring:\n  - Header: Back button + \"Settings\"\n  - Items:\n    1. **General** (`Language, History, Theme, System Font Scale`)\n    2. **Video** (`Pop-up play, screen orientation, continuous playback, HW/HW+ decoder`)\n    3. **Audio** (`Audio format, volume boost, clear voice, bass boost, equalizer`)\n    4. **Downloads** (`Path, max download tasks, UC turbo boost`)\n    5. **Subtitles** (`Appearance, font size, text color, sync delay`)\n    6. **Security & Private Vault** (`AES-256-GCM encryption, PIN lock, emergency calculator disguise`)\n    7. **About us** (`Version 2.4 PRO, hardware acceleration status, build info`)\n  - **Explicit User Constraint**: Do **NOT** add \"Game Center\" or \"Subscription\".\n- **Navigation Placement**: The Settings tab must be positioned **after Playlists** in the Android bottom navigation bar (making 5 bottom tabs: `Media`, `Browser`, `Downloads`, `Playlists`, `Settings`).\n\n---\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- **Active Workspace**: Vite + React 19 + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4.\n- `ActiveTab` in `src/types/index.ts` currently is `\'folders\' | \'browser\' | \'downloads\' | \'playlists\' | \'vault\'`. It needs `\'settings\'` added.\n- The `src/App.tsx` navigation bar currently renders 4 buttons (`folders`, `browser`, `downloads`, `playlists`).\n\n---\n\n### 5. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Update `src/types/index.ts`**:\n   - Change `ActiveTab` to include `\'settings\'`:\n     `export type ActiveTab = \'folders\' | \'browser\' | \'downloads\' | \'playlists\' | \'settings\' | \'vault\';`\n2. **Create `src/components/SettingsView.tsx`**:\n   - Implement the authentic Android MX Player settings layout based on the reference screenshot:\n     - Header: \"Settings\" with back arrow to return to Media tab.\n     - Section Rows with left icon, bold title, secondary text subtitle, and right chevron arrow:\n       - **General**: Phone/Tablet frame mode toggle, Dark/Light mode toggle, System adaptive font size (`Standard`, `Large`, `Extra Large`), Clear playback history.\n       - **Video**: Opens/integrates Video Enhancements (HW / HW+ / SW decoder, Dynamic Contrast, Saturation, Sharpness profile, Night comfort mode, Aspect ratio).\n       - **Audio**: Opens/integrates Audio Enhancements (Volume Boost up to 200%, Clear Voice dialogue enhancer, Bass boost, Spatial stereo, Equalizer preset, Bluetooth delay).\n       - **Downloads**: Default download path configuration, max concurrent tasks, Turbo Cloud acceleration toggle, \"Ask path before downloading\" toggle.\n       - **Subtitles**: Direct trigger for the Subtitle Customizer Modal.\n       - **Privacy & Security Vault**: Direct trigger for the AES-GCM Encrypted Private Vault and Emergency Calculator Disguise setup.\n       - **About us**: App title \"PlayThat! PRO v2.4\", Hardware acceleration engine status, open source video codec info.\n3. **Update `src/App.tsx`**:\n   - Import `SettingsView`.\n   - Render `SettingsView` when `activeTab === \'settings\'`.\n   - Add the **Settings** button to the bottom navigation bar (`<nav>`) placed immediately after `Playlists` (5-column grid: `grid-cols-5`).\n4. **Compile & Lint Verification**:\n   - Run `lint_applet` and `compile_applet` to confirm clean build.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- **Settings Screen Content**: Must follow the attached screenshot design (icon + title + subtitle + chevron) while explicitly **excluding** \"Game Center\" and \"Subscription\".\n- **Bottom Navigation Order**: Must be `Media` -> `Browser` -> `Downloads` -> `Playlists` -> `Settings`.\n- **Download Automation Rule**: Downloads must never start automatically without presenting the path/name confirmation prompt.\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_end: 277
