  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing UI Elements**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the UI elements within `src/App.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m examining the Android bottom navigation bar component. I\'ve begun to analyze the styling, particularly the use of Tailwind classes for height, padding, background, blur, border, and grid layout. My goal is to understand how these classes work together to achieve the final visual appearance.\n\n\n**Adding Settings Tab**\n\nI\'ve examined the bottom navigation bar and noted the existing tabs: Media, Browser, Downloads, and Playlists. The user\'s request is clear: I need to add a Settings tab after Playlists. I\'ve broken down the Settings UI from the attached image, focusing on the header (back arrow, title) and the list items. The list items will include General, Video, Audio, and Downloads, each with an icon, title, and subtitle.\n\n\n**Designing Settings Menu**\n\nI\'ve decided to incorporate an \"About us\" section with an info circle icon, the title \"About us,\" and the subtitle \"Fans group, official website, pages & channel.\" I will also include the settings for \"Subtitles\" and \"Security & Privacy\". I\'m planning out the styling for `SettingsView.tsx`, focusing on a dark background, a top app bar with a back button and the title \"Settings\", and a list.\n\n\n**Defining Interaction Details**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how users will interact with each setting item. I\'ve designed the visual style of setting sections with consistent stroke icons, titles, subtitles, and right chevrons. I\'m prioritizing user experience and interactivity, so tapping each item will either expand for details or open the respective controls screen. I\'m determining the best way to handle the General settings, including theme, display mode, font scale, language, and cache clearing. I\'m outlining controls for Video (decoder, sliders, aspect ratio) and Audio (volume boost) as well.\n\n\n**Implementing Audio Settings**\n\nI\'m now focusing on audio settings. I\'ve designed controls for a voice vocal enhancer, bass boost, spatial stereo, reverb, and an equalizer with presets like Flat, Bass Boost, and Vocal. I\'m also considering Bluetooth audio sync delay settings. I will then work on handling the Downloads tab, and the Subtitles and Security & Privacy settings.\n\n\n"
