  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Clarifying Top Bar Display**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the conditional rendering of the top header. Specifically, I\'m trying to determine whether the default \"PlayThat!\" header should be displayed when `activeTab` is \'settings\', or if the `SettingsView` should provide a custom MX Player settings top bar. I\'m leaning towards the latter.\n\n\n**Refining Settings Display**\n\nI\'ve decided to hide the top header when the `activeTab` is \'settings\'. This allows the `SettingsView` to render its own \"\342\206\220 Settings\" header directly below the status bar, matching the reference image. This approach also allows the bottom navigation bar to remain in place.\n\n\n"
