  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Request**\n\nI\'m starting to break down the user\'s request. It\'s becoming clearer: they want an app with a background-capable music player and notification controls. I\'m focusing on the core functionalities of background playback and notification integration. Now considering the architecture of this component.\n\n\n**Defining Core Features**\n\nI am now delving into the nitty-gritty, specifying features for a dedicated music player. I\'m imagining the user experience \342\200\223 a distinctive audio playback mode with album art, detailed song information, and comprehensive audio controls. It is essential to support background playback and allow interaction with the mini-player bar even while browsing other app sections, or while the phone is locked.\n\n\n**Implementing Background Playback**\n\nI\'m now implementing background music playback. I\'m focusing on the Web Audio API and HTML5 Audio element for a robust background pipeline. I\'m considering how this will work when a user minimizes or navigates away from the player tab, ensuring uninterrupted audio. I\'m also planning the user experience in mobile mode.\n\n**Incorporating Media Controls**\n\nNow, I\'m focusing on background controls. I\'m leveraging the Web `navigator.mediaSession` to control metadata and actions, enabling OS-level integration. I am implementing the notification shade, creating a native Android media player notification card for lock screen or background interaction. The goal is a seamless user experience.\n\n\n"
