  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Exploring Feature Implementations**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `audioPlayerService.ts` file. My goal is to determine how to build a background audio engine and notification system. I\'m thinking about how to manage audio tracks and the current track. My initial impressions of `AndroidFrame` are that it appears clean and well-structured.\n\n\n**Defining Audio State Management**\n\nI\'ve been drilling down on the intricacies of playback state. I plan to use the HTML5 `<audio>` element combined with the Web Audio API for gain boost. I\'m excited that this will seamlessly bind to the browser\'s `navigator.mediaSession`! I plan to populate the metadata and define action handlers for media controls and seek operations. I\'m also going to figure out reactive state subscription to update the UI on playback state changes.\n\n\n**Designing Lock Screen Integration**\n\nI\'m now contemplating how to integrate a mini-player into the lock screen experience. The goal is to build an Android-style lock screen with media controls, and I want to display the standard Android lock screen with a large digital clock, unlock prompts, the user\'s wallpaper, and a prominent Lock Screen Media Player widget. I want to let the user play/pause, scrub, skip, and adjust volume without unlocking the phone!\n\n\n"
