  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding Audio Tracks**\n\nI\'m focusing on incorporating high-quality, legal audio tracks into `src/data/sampleMedia.ts`. I\'m exploring open-source options like freemusicarchive, soundhelix, and archive.org audio demos, as well as Google Storage sample streams. The goal is to enrich the project with readily available, excellent audio resources.\n\n\n**Incorporating More SoundHelix Tracks**\n\nI\'ve gathered a diverse selection of SoundHelix tracks, specifically MP3s, for their browser compatibility. I am adding \"Synthwave Groove,\" \"Chill Acoustic,\" \"Cyberpunk Electronic,\" and \"Piano Ambient\" to the list. I\'m also considering integrating a FileBrowser filter to categorize \"Videos\" and \"Music/Audio\" or a dedicated \"Music\" folder for users\' audio. I\'ll need to check the `MediaItem` interface definition in `src/types/index.ts` next to plan the best data integrations!\n\n\n**Defining MediaItem Parameters**\n\nI\'ve updated the `MediaItem` interface with `artist`, `album`, and `mediaType` properties for richer audio file metadata. This should make it easier to manage and categorize different types of media files within the application. Next, I\'m setting my sights on the Audio & Notification System, starting with the implementation of `src/services/audioPlayerService.ts`. I\'m going to implement an HTML5 `<audio>` element with Web Audio API context for sound boosting. This approach supports uninterrupted background audio playback and full `navigator.mediaSession` integration.\n\n\n**Implementing Media Session**\n\nI\'ve integrated system-level background playback controls! I\'m now automatically updating `navigator.mediaSession.metadata` with track details and setting action handlers for play, pause, and track navigation. I also keep the playback state and position in sync. This setup offers mobile and desktop users background playback with lockscreen and notification controls. I\'m also including reactive event listeners to subscribe to state updates like `currentTrack`, `isPlaying`, `currentTime`, `duration`, `volume`, `isMuted`, `loopMode`, `isShuffle`, `queue`, and `queueIndex`.\n\n\n**Designing Android Media Controls**\n\nI am now focusing on integrating Android system controls in `AndroidFrame.tsx`. I\'m targeting the notification shade and lock screen with an Android 14/OneUI media player widget featuring album art, track details, scrubber, and playback controls. I also want to make sure the app plays music even when the phone is locked, providing a seamless user experience.\n\n\n**Designing Lockscreen Integration**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Android lockscreen media player, ensuring background audio playback. The phone lock screen will show the standard time and date, plus shortcuts. However, I\'m integrating a media player widget, featuring the album cover, track info, seek bar, and playback controls. Unlocking the phone smoothly transitions back to the application. I\'m also planning the design of a full music player modal and a floating mini player bar, which will be accessible from the bottom navigation.\n\n\n**Designing Full Music Player**\n\nI\'m working on a modern Android music player UI, inspired by apps like Samsung Music. I\'m focusing on the header with minimize, \"Now Playing,\" and queue list buttons. I\'m also planning the album art, track details with audio format badges, and an interactive seek bar with time indicators. I\'m also planning track controls!\n\n\n"
