  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Implementation Progress**\n\nI\'m pleased to report that the linting and compilation steps for the applet were successful. I\'ve now shifted focus to meticulously reviewing the user\'s requirements to ensure complete satisfaction. The initial assessment indicates that the direct MP4 video download functionality, mirroring a UC browser-like download manager, has been successfully implemented within `UCDownloadManager.tsx`.\n\n\n**Refining Functionality Details**\n\nI\'ve incorporated several key enhancements. Chunked parallel downloads, speed graphs, pause/resume, and Turbo multi-thread mode are implemented. The search bar is now full-width within `InAppBrowser.tsx`, the download manager is styled as \"PlayThat! Download Manager\". Multiple tabs are supported, up to 40, with grid view and quick switcher. The download prompt modal, in `DownloadPromptModal.tsx`, allows path customization and explicit start. Audio and video enhancement options are also added in settings.\n\n\n**Expanding Audio & Video Options**\n\nI\'ve added features for enhanced audio and video, like vocal clarity, a 200% volume boost, and both software and hardware video decoding with hardware acceleration. Equalizer presets and controls for video motion interpolation and aspect stretch are implemented. I\'m also addressing the font size issue; an adaptive system font scale setting has been incorporated, with CSS variable scaling for a seamless adjustment.\n\n\n**Implementing Background Music Playback**\n\nI\'ve just added a complete music player. `audioPlayerService.ts` leverages HTML5 Audio and Web Audio for background playback, even across tab navigation. I integrated `navigator.mediaSession` for OS lock screen and notification support, including metadata. I\'ve also built simulated Android Notification Shade and Lock Screen interfaces. These allow controls via the status bar, notification shade, or the simulated lock screen and lock button!\n\n\n"
