  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Observing Missing Code**\n\nI\'ve discovered a critical omission in `PrivateVaultModal.tsx`. The safety check, `if (!isOpen) return null;`, is entirely absent. This means that the modal component is attempting to render even when the `isOpen` prop, controlled in `App.tsx`, is set to `false`. This design flaw needs immediate attention.\n\n\n**Addressing Rendering Defect**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the `PrivateVaultModal`\'s persistent rendering issue. The fundamental flaw is the missing safety check: `if (!isOpen) return null;`. This oversight means the modal persists even when `isOpen` is false, and it needs a fix, especially when disguised.  I\'ve found that exiting the \"disguise\" mode via the `X` button doesn\'t close the modal. This critical conditional return must be implemented.\n\n\n"
