  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Modal Trigger**\n\nI\'m currently focused on how the `PrivateVaultModal` is triggered in `App.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m examining the `onOpenVaultModal` function, which sets `isVaultModalOpen` to `true`. This directly controls the modal\'s visibility. I\'m also reviewing lines 528-533, which render the modal based on this state variable. The `onClose` prop resets the state.\n\n\n**Refining Modal Behavior**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed a crucial issue: the modal in `PrivateVaultModal.tsx` was always rendering because there was no `if (!isOpen) return null;` condition. I\'m now investigating how to improve user experience by implementing escape key and backdrop clicks to close the modal. Also, considering the Calculator disguise mode, I\'m working on specific buttons to handle the \"exit disguise\" and close the vault functionalities properly. For Calculator mode, there must be a button to end the disguise, and another button to close the vault.\n\n\n"
