  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining a Clean Close**\n\nI\'m currently working in `PrivateVaultModal.tsx`. I\'ve just defined a `handleClose` helper function to neatly reset the modal\'s state. It addresses disguise, clears the PIN inputs, removes any error messages, and triggers the `onClose` callback for a clean exit.\n\n\n**Implementing Escape Key Exit**\n\nI\'ve just added an Escape key press listener within `PrivateVaultModal.tsx`, leveraging `useEffect` to manage the event. When the modal is open, pressing Escape now triggers `handleClose`, ensuring the modal can be dismissed cleanly via keyboard input. I\'ve also added a check right before rendering the modal, so it doesn\'t render when not open.\n\n\n**Refining Close Button Behavior**\n\nI\'ve just been refining the calculator disguise feature in `PrivateVaultModal.tsx`. I\'ve added a button that toggles the disguise mode, which shows the calculator instead of the vault. The close button is now also accessible in this state. It will call `handleClose` on exit.\n\n\n**Finalizing UI Interactions**\n\nI\'ve just ensured complete coverage of close actions in `PrivateVaultModal.tsx`. I\'ve added a button to exit the disguise mode, which seamlessly transitions back to the vault view, and added appropriate styling. I\'ve also incorporated a backdrop click handler that calls `handleClose` on click outside the vault. It should offer a clean exit from any context.\n\n\n"
