    response: "The close action on the Private Encrypted Vault has been resolved:\n\n### Cause & Resolution\n- **Issue**: `PrivateVaultModal` was missing the `if (!isOpen) return null;` render guard. When clicking the `\342\234\225` close button, the parent state was updating to `isOpen: false`, but the modal component continued rendering on screen.\n- **Fix**:\n  1. Added the `if (!isOpen) return null;` guard to ensure the modal unmounts immediately when closed.\n  2. Implemented `handleCloseModal()` to reset transient PIN input, clear errors, reset disguise mode, and call `onClose()`.\n  3. Added backdrop-click dismissal (clicking outside the dialog) and `Escape` keyboard dismissal.\n  4. Updated the Calculator disguise view so clicking `\342\234\225` or clicking outside cleanly closes the vault as well, with an inline button to toggle back to the vault view."
