  checkpoint {
    checkpoint_index: 2
    session_summary: "<summary>\n### 1. Task Overview\n- **User Request**: \n  1. Revamp the app color palette to use a combination of **Black, White, Grey, and Orange** (`#f97316` / `#ea580c` / orange accents).\n  2. Fix the visual issue where \"the current view got worse even the thumbnails are black and white\" \342\200\224 restore vivid, full-color video/audio thumbnails and replace dull all-monochrome styling with high-contrast dark theme (deep black `#000000`, slate/zinc greys, crisp white typography, and vibrant orange accents for active tabs, primary actions, progress bars, play buttons, and badges).\n- **Scope & Style Guidelines**: Follow `frontend-design` constitution: avoid generic slop, maintain WCAG AA contrast, make thumbnails natural/vibrant (remove any `grayscale` filters or black-and-white image URLs), and use orange as the signature accent across navigation, player controls, badges, and sliders.\n\n### 2. Progress\n- **Completed in Prior Turns**:\n  - Fixed `PrivateVaultModal.tsx` close behavior (`isOpen` guard, escape key handler, backdrop dismissal, and calculator disguise dismissal). Verified clean compilation and zero linter errors.\n  - Read `frontend-design` skill (`/skills/system_skills/frontend_design/SKILL.md`).\n- **In Progress / Current Turn**:\n  - User requested the color scheme update (Black + White + Grey + vibrant Orange accent) and restoring colored thumbnails across the app.\n\n### 3. Key Findings & Root Cause Analysis\n- **Thumbnails Issue**:\n  - Check `SAMPLE_MEDIA` in `/src/types.ts` or `/src/services/sampleData.ts` (or wherever sample media is initialized in `App.tsx` / `services/`). Check if Unsplash URLs or CSS classes have `grayscale`, `saturation-0`, or `?sat=-100` / `mono`.\n  - Look at `/src/components/FileBrowser.tsx`, `/src/components/VideoPlayer.tsx`, `/src/components/MiniMusicPlayer.tsx`, `/src/components/MusicPlayerModal.tsx`, `/src/components/PlaylistManager.tsx`, and `/src/components/UCDownloadManager.tsx` for any `grayscale` or `filter: grayscale` CSS utility classes applied to `<img>` or `<video>`.\n- **Palette Implementation (Black, White, Grey, Orange)**:\n  - Backgrounds: Deep blacks (`bg-black`, `bg-zinc-950`) and dark greys (`bg-zinc-900`, `bg-zinc-850`, borders `border-zinc-800`).\n  - Text: High contrast white (`text-white`) and soft greys (`text-zinc-300`, `text-zinc-400`).\n  - Signature Accent: Orange (`bg-orange-500`, `text-orange-500`, `hover:bg-orange-600`, `border-orange-500`, `accent-orange-500`, `fill-orange-500`).\n  - Active navigation indicators, progress bars, play icons, download indicators, and primary action buttons should feature the vibrant orange accent.\n\n### 4. Active Context\n- React + Vite SPA with Tailwind CSS.\n- Main entry point: `src/App.tsx`.\n- Key UI components to update:\n  - `src/App.tsx`: Bottom navigation bar active states (orange icons/text, active pill/pip indicator), stream modal button.\n  - `src/components/FileBrowser.tsx`: Video/audio thumbnail rendering (remove any grayscale filters), folder pills, search bar focus ring, play icons.\n  - `src/components/VideoPlayer.tsx`: Scrub bars, volume sliders, active decoder/track badges in orange.\n  - `src/components/MusicPlayerModal.tsx` & `src/components/MiniMusicPlayer.tsx`: Play/pause button, track progress bar, volume slider in orange.\n  - `src/components/UCDownloadManager.tsx`: Download progress meters, turbo boost badge, action buttons.\n  - `src/components/PlaylistManager.tsx`: Playlist cover thumbnails, active tracks.\n  - `src/components/AndroidFrame.tsx`: Status bar or subtle accents.\n  - `src/services/sampleData.ts` or `src/types.ts`: Ensure thumbnail URLs are rich, full-color film and music artwork (no grayscale params).\n\n### 5. Next Steps (In Priority Order)\n1. **Inspect Media & Thumbnail Sources**: Check `src/services/sampleData.ts` (or `src/types.ts` / `src/App.tsx`) and `src/components/FileBrowser.tsx` to find where thumbnails are rendered or filtered. Remove any `grayscale`, `filter`, or black-and-white Unsplash parameters. Replace any black/white placeholder image URLs with vibrant high-res movie/music artwork.\n2. **Apply Black, White, Grey & Orange Palette Across Core Components**:\n   - `FileBrowser.tsx`: Orange play buttons/hover accents, media badges, folder icons with orange tint or active indicators.\n   - `App.tsx`: Bottom navigation active tab highlighted in vibrant orange (`text-orange-500`, orange active indicator dot), header brand accent (e.g. orange dot or icon).\n   - `MiniMusicPlayer.tsx` & `MusicPlayerModal.tsx`: Orange progress bar, orange active shuffle/repeat/play button.\n   - `VideoPlayer.tsx`: Orange scrub bar timeline, orange volume bar, orange active playback speed indicator.\n   - `UCDownloadManager.tsx`: Orange download progress bar, orange boost badge.\n3. **Verify Build**:\n   - Run `lint_applet` (`tsc --noEmit`).\n   - Run `compile_applet` to verify zero build errors.\n\n### 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Must use the requested color combination: **Black, White, Grey, and Orange**.\n- Absolutely **no** black-and-white thumbnails: thumbnails must be full, rich color.\n- No dead buttons or placeholder stubs; preserve all working functionality (HLS streaming, crypto vault, UC downloader, audio player, gesture controls).\n</summary>"
    included_step_index_start: 277
    included_step_index_end: 336
    artifact_snapshots {
      artifact_name: "implementation_plan"
      artifact_absolute_uri: "file:///.aistudio/artifacts/brain/2c2ae0a3-e936-4ea4-824a-16ba79a755bd/implementation_plan.md"
