  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Security Mechanisms**\n\nI\'m now examining the security system\'s mechanics, specifically within `src/services/cryptoVault.ts`. Media encryption relies on AES-GCM, derived from a user-provided passkey (like a PIN). The next step is how we\'ll integrate the system PIN, fingerprint, or pattern for vault access.\n\n\n**Exploring Authentication Options**\n\nI\'ve been exploring a few authentication methods. WebAuthn with `navigator.credentials` looks promising, allowing secure key derivation. There\'s also Android\'s BiometricPrompt for fingerprint integration, which provides excellent user experience. I\'m additionally considering the 3x3 dot grid pattern lock for its ease of use and security, alongside a system PIN with a disguise calculator option. Finally, I\'m working on a lock type selector for user choice.\n\n\n**Defining Authentication Options**\n\nI\'m now concretizing the user\'s unlock options. It\'ll be a choice between fingerprint, PIN, and pattern unlock, configurable in settings. Users will be able to set up multiple methods, including fingerprint biometrics for all lock types! I\'m planning helper methods in `cryptoVault.ts` for managing pattern, primary auth method, biometrics enrollment, and authentication. I\'ll also be investigating how WebAuthn works.\n\n\n"
