  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Biometric Implementation**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `PrivateVaultModal.tsx` component. The key task is to integrate a robust Android biometric security system within it, supporting PIN, fingerprint, and other relevant authentication patterns. This involves leveraging Android\'s native biometric APIs for secure vault access.\n\n\n**Exploring Unlock Modalities**\n\nI\'m now diving into the specifics of three distinct unlock methods. Fingerprint integration involves a modern biometric prompt with animated feedback and WebAuthn calls where possible. PIN unlock incorporates a system keypad with a calculator disguise option. The pattern unlock utilizes an interactive 3x3 dot matrix with visual feedback and supports both setup and unlocking. A convenient switcher bar will be placed below for easy switching.\n\n\n**Designing Pattern Lock**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the 3x3 pattern lock. I\'m implementing the component inside `PrivateVaultModal.tsx`, using pointer events for interaction with 9 dots. Dragging across a dot adds it to the `selectedDots` array. SVG lines will be drawn connecting the dots. Orange accents will indicate active dots. Error messages will be shown for too few dots, requiring at least four to unlock. Finally, the pattern will be converted to a string.\n\n\n"
