  planner_response {
    response: "### Color Palette & Visuals (Black, White, Grey & Orange)\n- **Restored Natural Full-Color Thumbnails**: Removed all grayscale filters across the media browser, playlist manager, audio player, and notification cards. Movie and music thumbnails now render in rich, vibrant color.\n- **Vibrant Orange Signature Accents (`#f97316`)**:\n  - **Brand & Logo**: `PlayThat!` squircle chassis in dark slate with glowing orange soundwaves and play triangle.\n  - **Bottom Navigation**: Active tabs now illuminate with vibrant orange icons, text, and active indicator dots.\n  - **Player Controls**: Timeline scrub bars, soundwave visualizer bars, play buttons, and volume sliders now feature orange accents.\n  - **Badges & Modes**: `HW+` hardware acceleration badge, `PRO` indicator, active filter pills (All / Videos / Music), and UC Turbo Boost toggle all highlight in orange against deep black and dark grey surfaces.\n\n---\n\n### Private Vault Authentication (System PIN, Fingerprint & Pattern)\nThe Private Encrypted Vault now supports 3 authentication methods:\n\n1. **Fingerprint Biometrics (\360\237\221\206)**:\n   - Android-style biometric sensor with pulsating concentric orange glow rings and simulated haptic pulses (`navigator.vibrate`).\n   - Supports browser WebAuthn API with instant one-tap biometric verification.\n2. **3x3 Dot Grid Pattern Lock (\342\240\270)**:\n   - Interactive 3x3 Android pattern grid with live swipe and drag gesture tracking.\n   - Visual SVG connecting lines and glowing orange node indicators.\n   - Full setup flow (draw pattern $\\rightarrow$ confirm pattern) and unlock validation (minimum 4 dots).\n3. **System Numeric PIN (\360\237\224\242)**:\n   - 4-to-6 digit numeric keypad with glowing orange PIN dot indicators and backspace.\n   - Emergency calculator disguise mode (secret PIN + `=` shortcut).\n4. **Instant Unlock Switcher**:\n   - Tab strip right above the lock prompt to easily toggle between **Fingerprint**, **PIN**, and **Pattern**."
    thinking: "**Reviewing Recent Accomplishments**\n\nI\'m thrilled! Both `lint_applet` and `compile_applet` finished error-free. The major win this round was completely restoring rich, full-color thumbnails. Specifically, I removed all `filter grayscale` and `contrast-125` classes across `FileBrowser.tsx`. This change should significantly improve the user experience with more visually appealing previews.\n\n\n**Implementing Color Palettes**\n\nI\'ve been working on a new color palette implementation. I\'ve chosen a black, white, gray, and orange color scheme. Specifically, I\'m using black and dark grays for backgrounds, white for titles, and soft gray for metadata. The orange is being used for accents like the brand icon, active navigation tabs, media type filter pills, action buttons, and soundwave visualizers. This palette is already applied across `MiniMusicPlayer.tsx`, `MusicPlayerModal.tsx`, `PlaylistManager.tsx`, and `AndroidFrame.tsx`. All movie and music thumbnails now show in vivid, natural color.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### Color Palette & Visuals (Black, White, Grey & Orange)\n- **Restored Natural Full-Color Thumbnails**: Removed all grayscale filters across the media browser, playlist manager, audio player, and notification cards. Movie and music thumbnails now render in rich, vibrant color.\n- **Vibrant Orange Signature Accents (`#f97316`)**:\n  - **Brand & Logo**: `PlayThat!` squircle chassis in dark slate with glowing orange soundwaves and play triangle.\n  - **Bottom Navigation**: Active tabs now illuminate with vibrant orange icons, text, and active indicator dots.\n  - **Player Controls**: Timeline scrub bars, soundwave visualizer bars, play buttons, and volume sliders now feature orange accents.\n  - **Badges & Modes**: `HW+` hardware acceleration badge, `PRO` indicator, active filter pills (All / Videos / Music), and UC Turbo Boost toggle all highlight in orange against deep black and dark grey surfaces.\n\n---\n\n### Private Vault Authentication (System PIN, Fingerprint & Pattern)\nThe Private Encrypted Vault now supports 3 authentication methods:\n\n1. **Fingerprint Biometrics (\360\237\221\206)**:\n   - Android-style biometric sensor with pulsating concentric orange glow rings and simulated haptic pulses (`navigator.vibrate`).\n   - Supports browser WebAuthn API with instant one-tap biometric verification.\n2. **3x3 Dot Grid Pattern Lock (\342\240\270)**:\n   - Interactive 3x3 Android pattern grid with live swipe and drag gesture tracking.\n   - Visual SVG connecting lines and glowing orange node indicators.\n   - Full setup flow (draw pattern $\\rightarrow$ confirm pattern) and unlock validation (minimum 4 dots).\n3. **System Numeric PIN (\360\237\224\242)**:\n   - 4-to-6 digit numeric keypad with glowing orange PIN dot indicators and backspace.\n   - Emergency calculator disguise mode (secret PIN + `=` shortcut).\n4. **Instant Unlock Switcher**:\n   - Tab strip right above the lock prompt to easily toggle between **Fingerprint**, **PIN**, and **Pattern**."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 789618422
