  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Investigating Display Anomalies**\n\nI\'m currently focused on why the popup menu in Grid View only displays partially. My initial observation is that the parent `div` element has specific CSS classes like `overflow-hidden`. This could be the culprit, restricting the visible area. I\'m going to investigate how these styles interact with the popup\'s positioning and dimensions.\n\n\n**Refining Overflow Strategy**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the `overflow-hidden` class as the core issue, as predicted. It\'s clipping the popup menus that exceed the card\'s boundary. I am now exploring alternate approaches. Specifically, I\'m thinking about utilizing a bottom sheet modal on mobile devices, or a dropdown with `z-50` and `overflow-visible` on the parent card to ensure the menu is fully visible and interactive, especially with a backdrop that dismisses on click. I\'m testing the impact of removing `overflow-hidden` from the outer card.\n\n\n**Expanding Menu Solutions**\n\nI\'ve realized that the footer dropdown menus already bypass the `overflow-hidden` restriction. So, I\'m focusing on ensuring consistent behavior across views. I\'m adding a global backdrop that dismisses the active dropdown when clicked outside, using `activeMenuId` as a key. Also, I\'m now extending the three-dot action menu to the List View, mirroring its availability in Grid View, including mobile-specific bottom sheet or modal components to improve mobile user experience.\n\n\n**Implementing Interactive Menu**\n\nI\'m now implementing the interactive menu, leveraging a `selectedActionMedia` state to manage the selected item. Tapping the three dots will trigger an Android-style bottom action sheet on mobile or a centered modal on desktop, ensuring the menu is always fully visible with a `z-50` and no clipping. This design includes options like \"Add to Favorites\", \"Move to Private Vault\", and \"Delete File\". This is an ideal solution! I\'m also ensuring the PWA integration, as previously discussed, adding `usePWA`.\n\n\n"
