  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing UI Interactions**\n\nI\'m currently focused on improving the layout in `FileBrowser.tsx`, specifically when interacting with the three-dot menu on thumbnails. I\'ve pinpointed lines 270-452 as the relevant section to examine. I see we have the `activeMenuId` state variable to work with.\n\n\n**Refining Bottom Sheet Design**\n\nI\'m now implementing the bottom action sheet/modal for media item interactions. Instead of a simple string state for menu ID, I\'m using `selectedActionMedia` to store the actual `MediaItem` data, which should streamline actions. Clicking the three dots will now `stopPropagation`, set this `selectedActionMedia`, and trigger the visually appealing bottom sheet. The sheet includes a full header with media details and quick action buttons for playback, favoriting, moving to the private vault, and deleting.\n\n\n"
