  planner_response {
    response: "### 1. Fix for Three-Dots Menu Clipping\n- **Root Cause Identified**: The media card element had `overflow-hidden` with the menu positioned inside the card using `absolute bottom-full`. This caused the upper portion of the menu to be cut off by the card\'s bounding box.\n- **Solution Implemented**: \n  - Converted the menu into a **Mobile Action Sheet** (`fixed inset-0 z-50`) that overlays the screen with a dark backdrop. Because it renders at the root viewport layer, it cannot be clipped by card boundaries or scroll containers.\n  - Added the three-dots button to both **Grid View** and **List View**.\n  - The menu displays the file thumbnail, title, resolution, duration, and file size, with actions: **Play Now**, **Add to / Remove from Favorites**, **Move to Private Vault**, **Delete File**, and **Cancel**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Install This App on Your Phone\n\nYou can install **PlayThat! PRO** as a standalone app directly to your home screen with offline caching and full-screen gesture support.\n\n#### Option A: Quick 1-Tap from the App\n1. Tap the **\"Install\"** button with the phone icon in the top header or go to **Settings $\\rightarrow$ Install on Phone**.\n2. Tap **\"Install PlayThat! Now (1-Tap)\"** when prompted by your browser.\n\n#### Option B: On Android (Google Chrome / Edge / Brave)\n1. Open this link on your phone:\n   ```\n   https://ais-pre-mysyyuwzneh24y2ka6wxcs-69242674592.asia-east1.run.app\n   ```\n2. Tap the **three vertical dots (\342\213\256)** in the top-right corner of Chrome.\n3. Tap **\"Install app\"** or **\"Add to Home screen\"**.\n4. Confirm by tapping **\"Install\"**. The PlayThat! orange play icon will appear in your app drawer and home screen.\n\n#### Option C: On iPhone / iPad (Apple Safari)\n1. Open the app link in **Safari** on your iOS device.\n2. Tap the **Share** button (box with an upward arrow) in the bottom navigation bar.\n3. Scroll down and tap **\"Add to Home Screen\"** (`+` icon).\n4. Tap **\"Add\"** in the top-right corner.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Summary of Core Enhancements\n- **Color Palette**: High-contrast Black, White, Grey, and Orange (`#f97316`), with all video and music thumbnails in full color.\n- **Private Encrypted Vault**: Multi-factor unlock supporting **System PIN** (with Calculator disguise), **3x3 Dot Grid Pattern Lock**, and **Fingerprint Biometrics**.\n- **PWA Setup**: Web App Manifest, Service Worker caching, and high-resolution icons (`192x192`, `512x512`, `apple-touch-icon`, and maskable)."
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Display Issue**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the root cause. The grid item card\'s `overflow-hidden` property is conflicting with the absolute positioning of the popover. Specifically, the popover uses `absolute bottom-full mb-1`, which causes it to be truncated by the card\'s overflow behavior.\n\n\n**Refining the Popover Solution**\n\nI\'ve made significant progress. The overflow issue is resolved! I\'ve removed `overflow-hidden` from the grid item and implemented an Android-style Action Sheet Modal. It\'s fixed, covering the entire screen, and now includes a media preview, title, resolution, size, and duration. It also features \"Play Now,\" \"Add to Favorites,\" \"Move to Private Vault,\" \"Delete File,\" and a cancel button. I\'ve added the trigger to both Grid and List views.\n\nI am also working on PWA installation, and configured the infrastructure.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "### 1. Fix for Three-Dots Menu Clipping\n- **Root Cause Identified**: The media card element had `overflow-hidden` with the menu positioned inside the card using `absolute bottom-full`. This caused the upper portion of the menu to be cut off by the card\'s bounding box.\n- **Solution Implemented**: \n  - Converted the menu into a **Mobile Action Sheet** (`fixed inset-0 z-50`) that overlays the screen with a dark backdrop. Because it renders at the root viewport layer, it cannot be clipped by card boundaries or scroll containers.\n  - Added the three-dots button to both **Grid View** and **List View**.\n  - The menu displays the file thumbnail, title, resolution, duration, and file size, with actions: **Play Now**, **Add to / Remove from Favorites**, **Move to Private Vault**, **Delete File**, and **Cancel**.\n\n---\n\n### 2. How to Install This App on Your Phone\n\nYou can install **PlayThat! PRO** as a standalone app directly to your home screen with offline caching and full-screen gesture support.\n\n#### Option A: Quick 1-Tap from the App\n1. Tap the **\"Install\"** button with the phone icon in the top header or go to **Settings $\\rightarrow$ Install on Phone**.\n2. Tap **\"Install PlayThat! Now (1-Tap)\"** when prompted by your browser.\n\n#### Option B: On Android (Google Chrome / Edge / Brave)\n1. Open this link on your phone:\n   ```\n   https://ais-pre-mysyyuwzneh24y2ka6wxcs-69242674592.asia-east1.run.app\n   ```\n2. Tap the **three vertical dots (\342\213\256)** in the top-right corner of Chrome.\n3. Tap **\"Install app\"** or **\"Add to Home screen\"**.\n4. Confirm by tapping **\"Install\"**. The PlayThat! orange play icon will appear in your app drawer and home screen.\n\n#### Option C: On iPhone / iPad (Apple Safari)\n1. Open the app link in **Safari** on your iOS device.\n2. Tap the **Share** button (box with an upward arrow) in the bottom navigation bar.\n3. Scroll down and tap **\"Add to Home Screen\"** (`+` icon).\n4. Tap **\"Add\"** in the top-right corner.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Summary of Core Enhancements\n- **Color Palette**: High-contrast Black, White, Grey, and Orange (`#f97316`), with all video and music thumbnails in full color.\n- **Private Encrypted Vault**: Multi-factor unlock supporting **System PIN** (with Calculator disguise), **3x3 Dot Grid Pattern Lock**, and **Fingerprint Biometrics**.\n- **PWA Setup**: Web App Manifest, Service Worker caching, and high-resolution icons (`192x192`, `512x512`, `apple-touch-icon`, and maskable)."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 3
      nanos: 270223736
