  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining Component Tabs**\n\nI\'m currently reviewing the tabs within `PWAInstallModal.tsx`. I see on line 31 that the component currently uses a state variable `activeTab` to switch between \'android\', \'ios\', and \'qr\' tabs. I\'m focusing on adding an \'apk\' tab. It will be the recommended and default tab, so I\'m thinking through how to structure the UI update accordingly.\n\n\n**Defining APK Download Options**\n\nI\'ve decided on the labeling for the new \"Download .APK\" tab. I\'m structuring the options as follows: PWABuilder direct APK generation, Chrome WebAPK explanation (emphasizing that Chrome\'s \"Install\" function creates a legitimate `.apk`), and clear command-line instructions for building with Bubblewrap. I am providing a direct PWABuilder link, and making sure to call out Google TWA tool. I will then explain that the user can download the apk to their phone and install it using the file manager.\n\n\n"
    tool_calls {
