  planner_response {
    response: "The in-app install option was initially provided because modern Android devices use **WebAPK** (where Google Chrome compiles, signs, and registers an actual system `.apk` file directly on your phone when you tap \"Install\"). \n\nHowever, if you want a **standalone `.apk` file** to sideload, share, or install via Android Package Manager, the app now provides options to generate and download it:\n\n---\n\n### How to Get and Install the PlayThat `.apk` File\n\n#### Method 1: 1-Click .APK Package Generator (Recommended)\n1. Tap the **\"Get .APK\"** button in the top navigation bar (or open **Settings $\\rightarrow$ Get Android .APK / Install on Phone**).\n2. Select the **\"Download .APK\"** tab.\n3. Tap **\"Generate & Download PlayThat.apk\"** (powered by Microsoft & Google\'s official [PWABuilder](https://www.pwabuilder.com/reportcard?site=https%3A%2F%2Fais-pre-mysyyuwzneh24y2ka6wxcs-69242674592.asia-east1.run.app)).\n4. Tap **\"Generate APK\"** on the page. It will output a ready-to-install `playthat-pro.apk`.\n5. On your phone:\n   - Open your **Downloads** folder and tap the downloaded `.apk`.\n   - If prompted with *\"Install unknown apps\"*, toggle **Allow from this source**.\n   - Tap **Install**.\n\n---\n\n#### Method 2: Android Automatic WebAPK (No Manual Sideloading Required)\nIf you prefer not to configure unknown app permissions:\n1. Open this link on your phone in Google Chrome:\n   ```\n   https://ais-pre-mysyyuwzneh24y2ka6wxcs-69242674592.asia-east1.run.app\n   ```\n2. Tap the three dots (**\342\213\256**) in Chrome and tap **\"Install app\"**.\n3. Google Chrome\'s WebAPK minting service builds and installs an official `.apk` package (`org.chromium.webapk.*`) registered directly in Android Settings under **Apps**.\n\n---\n\n#### Method 3: Compile via Command Line (Bubblewrap CLI)\nIf you have Node.js and the Android SDK on your computer, you can build the `.apk` directly:\n```bash\nnpx @bubblewrap/cli init --manifest=https://ais-pre-mysyyuwzneh24y2ka6wxcs-69242674592.asia-east1.run.app/manifest.webmanifest\nnpx @bubblewrap/cli build\n```\nThis produces `app-release-signed.apk` ready to install via `adb install` or USB transfer."
    thinking: "**Clarifying Initial Display**\n\nI\'m now focusing on explaining the initial appearance of the in-app install prompt. My aim is to clearly illustrate that the web app operates within a cloud container using PWA/WebAPK standards. This enables Google Chrome to automatically generate and install a system `.apk` file on Android devices, without the necessity of manual sideloading.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "The in-app install option was initially provided because modern Android devices use **WebAPK** (where Google Chrome compiles, signs, and registers an actual system `.apk` file directly on your phone when you tap \"Install\"). \n\nHowever, if you want a **standalone `.apk` file** to sideload, share, or install via Android Package Manager, the app now provides options to generate and download it:\n\n---\n\n### How to Get and Install the PlayThat `.apk` File\n\n#### Method 1: 1-Click .APK Package Generator (Recommended)\n1. Tap the **\"Get .APK\"** button in the top navigation bar (or open **Settings $\\rightarrow$ Get Android .APK / Install on Phone**).\n2. Select the **\"Download .APK\"** tab.\n3. Tap **\"Generate & Download PlayThat.apk\"** (powered by Microsoft & Google\'s official [PWABuilder](https://www.pwabuilder.com/reportcard?site=https%3A%2F%2Fais-pre-mysyyuwzneh24y2ka6wxcs-69242674592.asia-east1.run.app)).\n4. Tap **\"Generate APK\"** on the page. It will output a ready-to-install `playthat-pro.apk`.\n5. On your phone:\n   - Open your **Downloads** folder and tap the downloaded `.apk`.\n   - If prompted with *\"Install unknown apps\"*, toggle **Allow from this source**.\n   - Tap **Install**.\n\n---\n\n#### Method 2: Android Automatic WebAPK (No Manual Sideloading Required)\nIf you prefer not to configure unknown app permissions:\n1. Open this link on your phone in Google Chrome:\n   ```\n   https://ais-pre-mysyyuwzneh24y2ka6wxcs-69242674592.asia-east1.run.app\n   ```\n2. Tap the three dots (**\342\213\256**) in Chrome and tap **\"Install app\"**.\n3. Google Chrome\'s WebAPK minting service builds and installs an official `.apk` package (`org.chromium.webapk.*`) registered directly in Android Settings under **Apps**.\n\n---\n\n#### Method 3: Compile via Command Line (Bubblewrap CLI)\nIf you have Node.js and the Android SDK on your computer, you can build the `.apk` directly:\n```bash\nnpx @bubblewrap/cli init --manifest=https://ais-pre-mysyyuwzneh24y2ka6wxcs-69242674592.asia-east1.run.app/manifest.webmanifest\nnpx @bubblewrap/cli build\n```\nThis produces `app-release-signed.apk` ready to install via `adb install` or USB transfer."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 380508810
    }
